response_content:
Tyson’s new daily distance  

\[
5000\ \text{m} + \frac{1}{5}\times 5000\ \text{m}
= 5000\ \text{m} + 1000\ \text{m}
= 6000\ \text{m}
\]

June has 30 days, so the total distance covered in June is  

\[
6000\ \text{m/day} \times 30\ \text{days}
= 180{,}000\ \text{m}
\]

**Answer: 180 000 meters (which is 180 km).**

Jack’s total time away from home is

\[
\text{Time to museum} + \text{Time at museum} + \text{Time back}
= \frac{150\text{ mi}}{75\text{ mph}} + 6\text{ h} + \frac{150\text{ mi}}{75\text{ mph}}
= 2\text{ h} + 6\text{ h} + 2\text{ h}
= 10\text{ hours}.
\]

**Answer: 10 hours.**

James reads at a constant rate:

- **Rate:** 10 minutes ÷ 3 pages = \(\frac{10}{3}\) minutes per page.

For 18 pages:

\[
18 \text{ pages} \times \frac{10}{3}\ \text{minutes per page}
= \frac{18 \times 10}{3}
= \frac{180}{3}
= 60 \text{ minutes}.
\]

**Answer: 60 minutes.**
